---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Turtle Transformation Limited"
  breadcrumb="Privacy Policy"
  description="GDPR-compliant data protection and privacy policy for Turtle Transformation Limited."
>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-sand-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <div class="border-b border-sand-200/80 pb-8 mb-10">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-turtle-700">Data Protection</span>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-normal text-turtle-950 mt-1 tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-sand-600 mt-2">Information on how personal data is processed in accordance with the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-sand-800 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">1. Controller Information</h2>
          <p>
            The data controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:<br><br>
            <strong>Turtle Transformation Limited</strong><br>
            Drom Upper, Glenbeigh, Co. Kerry, V93 F6X0, Ireland<br>
            Email: <a href="mailto:info@turtletrafo.com" class="text-turtle-800 underline underline-offset-2">info@turtletrafo.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">2. Overview of Data Processing</h2>
          <p>
            We process personal data only to the extent necessary to provide a functional, high-performance website and to respond to your inquiries regarding our coaching and consulting services.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">3. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
          <p>
            This website is statically hosted on GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub, Inc. (88 Colin P Kelly Jr St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you visit our website, GitHub may collect server log files, including your IP address, browser type, operating system, and timestamp of access. This processing is based on our legitimate interest in the secure and efficient provision of our website pursuant to Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">4. Direct Inquiries via Email</h2>
          <p>
            When you contact us via email (<a href="mailto:info@turtletrafo.com" class="text-turtle-800 underline underline-offset-2">info@turtletrafo.com</a>), your email address, name, and the details provided in your message are processed and stored solely for the purpose of handling your consultation inquiry and potential contract formation (Art. 6(1)(b) and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not share your contact information with third parties without your explicit consent.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">5. Cookies & Tracking</h2>
          <p>
            Our website is intentionally lightweight and privacy-respecting. We do not use advertising pixels or behavioral advertising cookies. Fonts are hosted on our own server; no data is sent to Google Fonts.
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-turtle-950 mt-4 mb-1">Google Analytics 4 (only with your consent)</h3>
          <p>
            If you click &ldquo;Accept&rdquo; in the cookie banner, we use Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service provided by Google Ireland Limited (Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland). Google Analytics sets cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, stored for up to 2 years) and collects pseudonymous usage data such as pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser information. Google may transfer this data to the United States; such transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and/or Standard Contractual Clauses. We do not enable advertising features or share the data for advertising purposes.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Legal basis: your consent pursuant to Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and the corresponding national rules on storing information on your device. Without your consent, no connection to Google Analytics servers is established and no analytics cookies are set. Your choice is stored in your browser (local storage) so we do not ask again on every visit.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You can withdraw or change your consent at any time with the &ldquo;Cookie settings&rdquo; link in the page footer. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-turtle-950 mt-4 mb-1">YouTube video testimonials (only when activated)</h3>
          <p>
            Video testimonials do not connect to YouTube when the page loads. A connection to YouTube is made only when you choose to play a testimonial. This can transmit personal data, such as your IP address and device or browser information, to YouTube. This choice is separate from your Google Analytics cookie consent.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">6. Your Rights Under GDPR</h2>
          <p>
            Under the GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your personal data:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sand-700 mt-2">
            <li>Right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Right to erasure / &ldquo;Right to be forgotten&rdquo; (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To exercise any of these rights, simply email us at <a href="mailto:info@turtletrafo.com" class="text-turtle-800 underline underline-offset-2">info@turtletrafo.com</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Irish Data Protection Commission (DPC) or your competent supervisory authority.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-turtle-950 mb-2">7. Updates to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect operational or regulatory changes. The latest version will always be accessible on this page.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs text-sand-500 mt-2">Last updated: October 2026</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
